each staff member’s own permissions also apply.\n\nDelegated administrationCo-managed SLA priorities\nCustomer-approved access\n\nOversight of the initial service desk board\n\nBoards\n\nService Desk: Collaborate\n\nProjects\nStaff\n\nNo access configured.\n\nSearch\nSelect an item\nSelect...\nAdd\nTeams\n\nNo access configured.\n\nSearch\nSelect an item\nSelect...\nAdd\nSave access\nReload current access\nCo-managed SLA priorities\n\nMap customer priorities to MSP priorities. New escalations use your client, board, or default SLA policy. Existing clocks keep their targets.\n\nAccess settings saved.\n\nConfigure an MSP SLA policy before escalation.\nManage SLA policies\nMSP priority for Low\nWhimsical Wish\nMSP priority for Critical\nWhimsical Wish\nMSP priority for Medium\nWhimsical Wish\nMSP priority for High\nWhimsical Wish\nMSP priority for Urgent\nWhimsical Wish\nSave access\nReload current access\nDelegated administration\n\nCustomer-approved assistance with selected settings and user records.\n\nRefresh access\nCustomer workspace: CM-REVIEW-20261026-01 Accept-3 IT · MSP: Oz\n\nNo administration tasks are currently approved.\n\nShared tickets\nFilters\nView\n\n0 tickets · 0 open · 0 closed\n\nNo customer tickets to show yet.\n\nOpen in Customer Tickets\nWork\n\nClient projects and shared task queues stay in the MSP shell with their qualified identities.\n\nProjects\nProject task queues\nEnd co-management\n\nReview what happens when this relationship ends.\n\nCM-REVIEW-20261026-01 Accept-3 IT\n\nLive access between these organizations ends immediately when you confirm.\n\nThe customer keeps its workspace and data. Read access, export, and upgrade to an independent AlgaPSA subscription remain available.\n\nThe MSP retains its own records and permitted historical evidence of shared work it participated in.\n\nAllocated co-managed seats return to the MSP’s pool. This does not cancel subscriptions or delete either workspace.\n\nReview departureRefresh status",
